% This is a placeholder for the excitation controller Simulink subsystem.
% In a real MATLAB/Simulink environment, this would contain the Stateflow chart
% implementing the adaptive supervisory logic for excitation control.

% The subsystem should implement:
% - State machine: IDLE -> EXCITE -> ESTIMATE -> EVALUATE_UNCERTAINTY ->
%   {CONVERGED | NOT_CONVERGED} -> (back to EXCITE or IDLE)
% - Adaptive control logic based on parameter estimation uncertainty
% - Safety limits for excitation amplitude, width, and rate
% - Interface with parameter estimator for uncertainty feedback
%
% Inputs:
% - Parameter estimates [R0_est, R1_est, C1_est]
% - Parameter uncertainties [R0_unc, R1_unc, C1_unc] or covariance metrics
% - Estimation convergence flag
% - Safety limits (max amplitude, max width, max duty cycle)
% - Cycle timing signals
% - Manual override signals
%
% Outputs:
% - Excitation amplitude command
% - Excitation width command
% - Excitation period command
% - Estimator reset signal
% - Hold/reduce rate signal
% - Current state indicator (for monitoring/diagnostics)
%
% States:
% - IDLE: Waiting for start signal, outputs zero/minimal excitation
% - EXCITE: Applying excitation pulse with current parameters
% - ESTIMATE: Waiting for parameter estimation to complete
% - EVALUATE_UNCERTAINTY: Checking if estimates have converged
% - CONVERGED: Parameters have converged; optionally hold or reduce excitation rate
% - NOT_CONVERGED: Parameters not converged; increase amplitude/rate (within limits)
%
% Adaptive Logic:
% - If uncertainty high -> increase excitation amplitude to improve SNR
% - If uncertainty medium -> maintain current excitation level
% - If uncertainty low -> can decrease excitation to save energy
% - Also adjust repetition rate based on convergence speed
% - Apply rate limiting and safety constraints
%
% This file represents the intended structure. Actual implementation requires
% using MATLAB Simulink and Stateflow editors to create:
% - Stateflow graphical state machine with the specified states and transitions
% - MATLAB Function blocks for adaptive logic computations
% - Gain blocks for applying limits and scaling
% - Memory blocks for storing previous cycle parameters
% - Output ports for excitation parameters and control signals